# == Frazaro / VLA English ==

# Build artifact - rebuilt any time by VlaBuildAddin (DEPLOY.md);
# the .bas sources in this repo are the truth, the add-in is output.
# (Named VLA_English.xlam before V5.1, then Frazaro.xlam before
# EDITIONMANIFEST.2's rename to Frazaro_English.xlam; all three stay
# ignored so an old artifact on disk never sneaks into history.)
Frazaro.xlam
Frazaro_English.xlam

# EDITIONMANIFEST.1: every other edition's own build artifact, same
# reasoning - add one line per edition VlaEditionNames knows about.
Frazaro_Espanol.xlam

# VlaRefreshBetaCopy's own "Personal dev convenience" Register-for-
# Auto-Load test copy (VLA_Build.bas) - same rebuilt-any-time output as
# Frazaro.xlam above, just under its own name; noticed untracked after
# a live rebuild, not previously covered.
Frazaro_Beta.xlam

# DI.3a: generated by VlaBuildAddin from VLA.bas's VLA_RELEASE_VERSION -
# same "source in the repo, output is not" split as Frazaro.xlam above.
installer/version.iss
installer/output/

# PORT.4: the Cargo workspace's build output (core/, cli/), including the
# wasm core that tools/check_core_imports.ps1 reads. Cargo.lock is NOT
# ignored: the workspace has a binary, so the lockfile is committed once a
# toolchain has written it.
target/

# PORT.6 (slice 6h): the web page tools/build_web.ps1 writes from
# web/index.template.html, the wasm core, the prelude and english.vla - the
# same "source in the repo, output is not" split as Frazaro_English.xlam.
web/index.html

# KERNEL.3: the benchmark page tools/bench_view.ps1 writes from
# tools/bench_view.template.html and a view record of a synthetic program -
# the same split: the template is source, the filled page is output.
tools/bench_view.html

# Excel lock/temp files (appear while a workbook is open)
~$*
*.tmp
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
# PORT.7 (slice 7a): the build golden, the one workbook the repository
# keeps. The writer's oracle is its own bytes (conformance/README.md, the
# amendment of 2026-10-03), opened by the owner in Excel; *.xlsx stays
# ignored everywhere else, and a later fixture under scripts/build/ joins
# this one by the same rule.
!scripts/build/*.xlsx
# PORT.8 (slice 8a): the reader's fixtures, by the same rule - the
# workbooks under scripts/reflect/ whose relations are the goldens of the
# treaty's oracle 8, each opened by the owner in Excel.
!scripts/reflect/*.xlsx
# KERNEL.3 (the study before the viewport): the study's fixtures, by the
# same rule - the workbooks under scripts/study/ that
# tools/build_study_fixture.ps1 writes, their planted defects the answer
# key of docs/PROTOCOL.md, each opened by the owner in Excel.
!scripts/study/*.xlsx
# KERNEL.7 (recalculation): the subset's fixture, by the same rule - the
# workbook under scripts/recalc/ that frazaro build writes from subset.txt,
# one formula per function the declared subset computes, and the owner's
# save of it from Excel 365 beside it, whose cached values are the oracle.
!scripts/recalc/*.xlsx
# The dev workbook VLA.xlsm is deliberately NOT tracked (untracked at the
# 0.5.0 public import; it was the tracked "lab bench" before). It is a
# blank workbook plus the imported modules - rebuilt from nothing in three
# steps, see docs/TESTING.md "The lab bench, from nothing" - and it
# accumulates session residue (the VLA_Log parse-failure sheet, VLAu_*
# undo snapshots) that must never be published, plus a multi-megabyte
# binary diff every session that must never be in history.

# Scratch area for throwaway test workbooks - keep experiments here
# so they never clutter history.
scratch/
archive/
screenshots/

# docs/archive/ is a DIFFERENT thing wearing the same folder name as
# the throwaway scratch archive/ above: permanent documentation
# history (old ALPHA*_ROADMAP.md files) meant to stay in git forever,
# not scratch content meant to stay out of it. Carved back out of the
# blanket archive/ rule so it doesn't silently vanish from tracking.
!docs/archive/
!docs/archive/**
